# AI Study Companion — 7-Day Implementation Plan

**Role:** Lead Software Architect & AI/ML Specialist
**Team:** 1 SDE (Backend/Infra) + 1 AI/ML Intern (Model/Pipeline), working in parallel tracks that converge each day
**Stack:** FastAPI · PostgreSQL · Redis · ChromaDB (vector store) · React (frontend) · LLM API (Claude/OpenAI)
**Scope for this sprint:** The core loop — **Adaptive Study Planner → Session Focus Tracking → AI Quiz Generator**, plus the **RAG Doubt Solver**, wired to a working frontend.

---

## How to Use This Plan

- Each day has a **hard cutoff**: the End-of-Day Verification must pass before Day N+1 starts. If it doesn't, Day N+1's morning is spent fixing Day N, not starting new work.
- The SDE owns everything under `app/` (API, DB, infra). The AI/ML Intern owns everything under `ai_service/` (pipelines, prompts, model logic) and exposes it as **plain Python functions with typed inputs/outputs** — never FastAPI routes directly. The SDE wraps those functions in routes. This is the seam that lets both people work without blocking each other.
- Contract-first: any endpoint or function signature the two of you will share is written down (as a Pydantic model or function stub) **before** either of you implements it, ideally at the start of Day 1.

