## Day 1 — Foundations: Skeleton, Contracts, Data Pipeline Bootstrap

### Objective
Stand up a running FastAPI app with a real database connection and CI-ready structure; in parallel, get raw study content flowing through a preprocessing pipeline the AI features will depend on all week.

### SDE Tasks
- Initialize the repo with the directory structure above; `app/main.py` boots a FastAPI app with a `/health` endpoint.
- Set up `docker-compose.yml` with `postgres`, `redis`, and `chroma` services.
- Configure `core/config.py` (pydantic-settings, reads `.env`) and `core/database.py` (SQLAlchemy engine + `SessionLocal`).
- Define initial SQLAlchemy models: `User`, `Subject`, `Topic`, `StudyPlan`, `PlanItem`.
- Set up Alembic and generate/apply the first migration.
- Write the **Pydantic contract stubs** for Day 2–4 endpoints (`schemas/plan.py`, `schemas/quiz.py`, `schemas/doubt.py`) even though the logic isn't built yet — this is what the Intern codes against.

### AI/ML Intern Tasks
- Set up `ai_service/` package with a working Python environment (`pip install -r ai_service/requirements.txt`: `openai`/`anthropic` SDK, `chromadb`, `tiktoken`, `pypdf`).
- Build `preprocessing/chunker.py`: splits raw text/PDF notes into overlapping chunks (~500 tokens, ~50 token overlap) with `chunk_text(text: str) -> list[str]`.
- Build `preprocessing/cleaner.py`: strips whitespace/artifacts from OCR or pasted notes.
- Write a standalone script (`ai_service/scripts/test_pipeline.py`) that loads 2–3 sample text files, cleans, chunks, and prints chunk counts/token estimates.
- Confirm access to the chosen LLM API key works with a trivial "hello world" completion call, logged to console.

### Implementation Guidelines
- **Pattern:** Router → Service → Model. Routers never touch SQLAlchemy directly; they call a service function.
- **Libraries:** `fastapi`, `uvicorn[standard]`, `sqlalchemy`, `alembic`, `pydantic-settings`, `psycopg2-binary`.
- **Config:** all secrets/URLs via `.env`, never hardcoded. Commit `.env.example` only.
- **AI/ML side:** keep every function pure (no FastAPI imports in `ai_service/`) — this is what makes Day 4's integration painless.

### End-of-Day Verification
```bash
# SDE
docker compose up -d postgres redis chroma
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
curl -s http://localhost:8000/health          # expect {"status":"ok"}
alembic upgrade head                            # migration applies cleanly
psql $DATABASE_URL -c "\dt"                     # tables exist: users, subjects, topics, study_plans, plan_items

# AI/ML Intern
python ai_service/scripts/test_pipeline.py      # prints chunk counts, no errors
python -c "from ai_service.embeddings.embed import test_llm_connection; test_llm_connection()"  # confirms API key works
```
**Gate to Day 2:** `/health` returns 200, migrations applied, and the pipeline script runs end-to-end with no exceptions.

