## Day 5 — Frontend Scaffolding & Core API Integration

### Objective
A working React app can register/login, view a plan, start a session, and see quiz questions rendered — the AI/ML Intern shifts to hardening and edge cases while the SDE focuses on frontend wiring.

### SDE Tasks
- Scaffold `frontend/` with Vite + React + a typed API client (`frontend/src/api/client.ts` using `axios` or `fetch` wrappers, one function per endpoint).
- Build pages: `LoginPage`, `PlannerPage` (list plan items), `SessionPage` (start/end session button + score display), `QuizPage` (renders questions, submits answers).
- Store JWT in memory/`localStorage` (documented as a known simplification — flag for future httpOnly-cookie hardening) and attach it via an axios interceptor.
- Add `.env` for `VITE_API_BASE_URL` so frontend/backend can run independently.

### AI/ML Intern Tasks
- Stress-test `generate_quiz` and `answer_doubt` against 15–20 varied topics/questions; log failures (malformed JSON, empty answers, off-topic drift) in a `known_issues.md`.
- Tune `prompts/quiz_prompt.py` and `prompts/doubt_prompt.py` based on failures found.
- Add input length guards (reject/truncate notes over a token limit before chunking) to prevent oversized-context errors.
- Start on the "explain like I actually don't get it" mode stub: `generation/doubt_solver.py::answer_doubt_alternate_style(question, context, prior_attempts)` — logic only, not wired into the API yet.

### Implementation Guidelines
- **Frontend pattern:** one API function per backend endpoint in `api/`, one hook per page (`usePlan()`, `useSession()`, `useQuiz()`) — no direct fetch calls inside components.
- **CORS:** enable `CORSMiddleware` in `app/main.py` for `http://localhost:5173` during dev.
- **Error surfacing:** every API hook catches errors and surfaces a user-readable message; never a blank screen on failure.

